TEST: -L is approximation, never silently dropped
INPUT_DISPLAY: 'screen' '--dry-run' '-L'
ACTUAL_EXIT: 3
OUTPUT_DISPLAY_BEGIN
screen2tmux: APPROX: Screen -L enables Screen's built-in logging policy; tmux has no matching startup logging flag and pipe-pane only covers selected panes unless additional hooks are installed.
screen2tmux: suggestion: Closest initial-pane substitute: create the session, then run tmux pipe-pane -o 'cat >>tmux.log'; add after-new-window/after-split-window hooks if automatic logging of future panes is required.
OUTPUT_DISPLAY_END
OUTPUT_HEX: 
==============================================================================
TEST: -Logfile without -L is unsupported
INPUT_DISPLAY: 'screen' '-Logfile' '/tmp/screen.log' '--dry-run'
ACTUAL_EXIT: 2
OUTPUT_DISPLAY_BEGIN
screen2tmux: UNSUPPORTED: Screen -Logfile stores a default logfile name even when logging is not yet enabled; tmux pipe-pane has no equivalent persistent logfile-name setting.
screen2tmux: suggestion: Create the tmux session normally, then use pipe-pane with an explicit destination whenever logging is enabled.
OUTPUT_DISPLAY_END
